+## 2026-11-20 (Nitto ATP Finals highlights missing / on the wrong match — data repaired, code NOT fixed yet)
+
+Ask: Tennis TV (`@tennistv`) videos for the Nitto ATP Finals singles and doubles were not showing up on breakpoint.zone. Two separate causes, both in `api/match-highlights/sync.ts`. **This session repaired the data in Supabase only; no code was changed or deployed, and the repaired rows will be overwritten again by the sync unless the code is fixed first (see "Time-sensitive").**
+
+### Cause 1 — the live-match gate skips the post-match upload window (confirmed from code + write timestamps)
+
+`sync.ts` returns `{ skipped: true, reason: 'no_live_atp_wta_match' }` unless `get_livescore` shows an ATP/WTA match live *right now* (`hasLiveAtpWtaMatch`). Tennis TV uploads highlights 30 min to ~3 h *after* a match ends, so evening uploads land when nothing is live and are not pulled until the next day's first live match. Evidence: the cron is `*/30` and `match_highlights` POSTs from the sync (Supabase edge logs) show two per hour all day Nov 19, then the last one at 21:00 UTC and nothing at 21:30 or after. Three Finals videos uploaded later were missing: `IFwl5Y_uTdo` (21:42), `zYNf3gxdSPI` (22:00), `Fa0j6w3wMx4` (23:03). The skip is silent (200, no log line), which is why nothing looked broken.
+
+### Cause 2 — the refresh pass re-matches old videos against only yesterday+today's fixtures (high confidence; the exact fixture payloads were not inspected)
+
+Each tick re-fetches metadata for every row from the last 3 days (`recentKnownRows`) and **upserts `tournament_key`, `event_type_type`, `match_id`, `match_label`, `match_confidence` again** using `matchVideoToFixture(title, candidates)`, where `candidates` come from `fetchRecentFixtures()` = yesterday..today only. So a Day 2 "Alcaraz vs Tiafoe" video re-synced on Day 4 is matched against Day 3/4 fixtures, where only "Alcaraz v Medvedev" contains Alcaraz, and is rewritten as a `probable` link to that match. Same for Fils/Jodar clips re-synced on Day 5 (landed on "Shelton v Jodar"). Related defects in the same function:
+- Ties go to the first candidate (`surnameHits > best.surnameHits`, strict). A daily recap naming four players ties 2-2-2 and gets `confirmed` on whichever fixture is first (e.g. the Day 3 recap "Fils-Jodar Battle, Zverev Takes on Shelton" was `confirmed` on Shelton v Jodar).
+- No day awareness: a video's publish date is never compared with a fixture's `event_date`.
+- If no candidate matches and the title has no tournament alias, the row is rewritten with `tournament_key = null`, which removes it from the tournament card (the API filters by `tournament_key` + `event_type_type` + `day`).
+- `confirmed` is what the UI shows as a match label (`VideoList.tsx`, `PlayingPane.tsx`; `api/match-highlights/{index,recent}.ts` only expose `matchLabel` when `confirmed`). `probable` only affects ranking.
+
+### What was done this session (Supabase `Breakpoint - Fun Facts`, table `match_highlights`; not in git)
+
+1. **Inserted 3 missing videos**, `status = 'published'`: `IFwl5Y_uTdo` and `Fa0j6w3wMx4` on 12179706 Zverev v Fils (`confirmed`), `zYNf3gxdSPI` (Day 5 recap, `daily`) on 12179704 Shelton v Jodar (first-named match, `probable`). Compared ~60 recent channel uploads with the table: these were the only missing 2026 Finals match videos; doubles Days 1-5 were complete. Practice sessions, pre-event press conferences and archive replays were not treated as match videos.
+2. **Re-linked 58 singles rows** to the match actually played that day. Script: `docs/handoff-2026-11-20/relink_singles.sql` (idempotent; schedule and rules are in its header). Undo: `docs/handoff-2026-11-20/rollback_relink.sql`. Singles schedule used (one match per player per day): Nov 15 Zverev-Jodar 12179707, Shelton-Fils 12179703; Nov 16 Alcaraz-Tiafoe 12179698, Medvedev-Cobolli 12179701; Nov 17 Fils-Jodar 12179700, Zverev-Shelton 12179705; Nov 18 Alcaraz-Medvedev 12179696, Cobolli-Tiafoe 12179699; Nov 19 Shelton-Jodar 12179704, Zverev-Fils 12179706. After: Alcaraz v Medvedev 15, Alcaraz v Tiafoe 13, Cobolli v Tiafoe 9, Fils v Jodar 11, Medvedev v Cobolli 2, Shelton v Fils 12, Shelton v Jodar 12, Zverev v Fils 12, Zverev v Jodar 6, Zverev v Shelton 11.
+3. **Doubles links were not audited or changed** (per-day doubles fixture IDs are not known). Known wrong example: `HYeAEWw_Cu8` "Luz Goes Around The Net" (Nov 16) is on 12179713 Arevalo/Pavic v Luz/Matos (a Nov 19 match). Known IDs: 12179708 Arribage/Olivetti v Luz/Matos, 12179709 Heliovaara/Patten v Arevalo/Pavic, 12179710 Heliovaara/Patten v Arribage/Olivetti, 12179713, 12179715 Harrison/Skupski v Bolelli/Vavassori.
+
+### Time-sensitive: the repair will be partly undone
+
+The group-2 matches (Alcaraz, Medvedev, Cobolli, Tiafoe) play their last round-robin matches on Nov 20, so the gate opens when the first one goes live (~13:00 UTC). The next tick then re-matches every row published since ~Nov 17 against Nov 19-20 fixtures (Cause 2) and overwrites most of the 58 re-linked rows (and can null the match fields of Day 3/4 rows). Rows from Nov 15-16 fall outside the 3-day refresh and keep their repair. **Merge the fix below before then, or re-run `relink_singles.sql` after each tick until it is merged.**
+
+### Suggested fix (proposed, not implemented — nothing below is in the repo)
+
+1. **Refresh must not rewrite match fields.** For rows already in `match_highlights`, upsert only metadata (`title`, `view_count`, `duration_seconds`, `thumbnail_url`, `embeddable`, `updated_at`); compute `tournament_key` / `event_type_type` / `match_*` only for video IDs not already in the table, or only overwrite when the existing `match_confidence` is `unknown` and the new one is better. This alone stops the clobbering.
+2. **Day-aware candidates.** Build candidates from fixtures for the video's own publish date (and the previous day) instead of "yesterday..today now", or at least compare `event_date` to `deriveDay(publishedAt)`; fetch fixtures for each distinct day in the batch.
+3. **Ties.** If two candidates tie on `surnameHits`, do not pick the first: return `probable`/`unknown`, or for dailies leave `matchId` null.
+4. **Post-match grace window in the gate.** Open the gate if a live ATP/WTA match exists OR an ATP/WTA fixture started in the last ~12 h (use `event_date` + `event_time` with `timezone: 'UTC'`; add them to `RawFixture`). Quota impact is small (~17 YouTube units per tick). Also `console.log` a line when skipping, so a silent gate is visible in Vercel logs.
+5. Tests live in `api/match-highlights/sync.test.ts` (426 lines) and already cover `matchVideoToFixture` and the gate helpers; add cases for the tie and for re-syncing an old video against a newer fixture list.
+
+### Run from the Mac
+
+1. `git pull` on this repo (this entry and `docs/handoff-2026-11-20/` arrive with it).
+2. Confirm the gate behaviour: `curl -s -H "Authorization: Bearer $CRON_SECRET" https://www.breakpoint.zone/api/match-highlights/sync` (expect `{"skipped":true,"reason":"no_live_atp_wta_match"}` before the first Nov 20 match goes live).
+3. Implement the fix above (item 1 is the one that matters before ~13:00 UTC), `npm test`, ship per the repo's usual PR flow.
+4. After the first live tick, check the damage: `select match_label, count(*) from match_highlights where tournament_key = 2794 and published_at >= '2026-11-15' and match_label is not null group by 1 order by 1;` and compare with the counts above. If it drifted, run `docs/handoff-2026-11-20/relink_singles.sql` (Supabase SQL editor; add Nov 20 fixtures to its `VALUES` list first).
+5. For the semifinals and final, add their match IDs/dates to `relink_singles.sql` if the fix is not merged by then.
+
+### Process notes for next time
+
+- The cloud session first had only the wrong repo (`bgoldenberg/breakpoint-zone`, README + screenshots) and found the pipeline from Supabase edge logs (`mcp__Supabase__query_logs`, `source='edge_logs'`, filter `event_message like '%match_highlights%'`, group by hour) before the right repo was attached. Vercel runtime logs only hold ~1 h on this plan and the sync logs nothing when it skips.
+- A stray `handoff/` folder (an earlier copy of this entry plus the same SQL) exists on branch `claude/fervent-cray-rm8zj0` of `bgoldenberg/breakpoint-zone`; safe to delete.
+- Write access to this repo was not granted to the cloud session, so this entry was delivered as a patch (`git am`), not a push.
